<section class="container" style="padding-block:4rem 2rem;max-width:760px;">
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Most communication projects start with the means: a campaign, a relaunch, a website. The tool is fixed before the task is clear. Here the order is reversed — the starting point is the decision that is supposed to be made at the end, and everything else follows backwards from it.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">This is not a matter of style but a response to a changed situation: execution — design, copy, images, code — has become fast and cheap. What has remained scarce is the well-founded decision about what to do and what to leave out, and the willingness to stand by it.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-2">What matters is the concept — and securing the right placement in the market, with maximum credibility and persuasive power.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">This sentence contains four statements. Each has its own page.</p>
</section>

